{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/786803-ideas-for-building-a-campaign-setting","id":786803,"title":"Ideas for building a campaign setting.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-15T11:08:42-08:00","id":786803,"title":"Ideas for building a campaign setting.","content":"Once again, I am trying to launch a Scion game for my friends. Usually, my previous attempts collapsed because I couldn't form a coherent storyline, but this time, I have three big arcs, one for each power level. These are still three very broad ideas, but I really like them, and I want to find a way to link them together logically.<br /> <br /> For Hero : The Band's adventures will take place in a Sunnydale-like city. It seems like the usual student town, but when you scratch the surface, you find that a lot of legendary creatures, Titanspawns and such lives there. I want to have an 'adventure of the week' feel, so we can focus on recurring NPCs, relationships, building characters and backgrounds... This town is actually a inter-pantheon project, some sort of secret training grounds for Scions. They're unaware of that, and most creatures have forgotten that, but the city has Legend in itself, and Fate has taken a particular interest in it. Which means that I can gradually go wild on it, since one of the specifics of this special town is that it always keeps a stable population. Even if people are being secretly sacrificed by Aztec Scions, or a whole district suffers a plague, somewhere in the country (probably the USA), people are suddenly compelled to move there, to replace the numbers.<br /> <br /> For Demigod : Somehow, the Band will die. But they will be brought back with other Scions in a giant virtual simulation, very heavily inspired by The World Ends With You, and forced to play in a series of extreme scenarios to earn points, so the winner(s?) can be eventually brought back to life for real. The gods will be running this, and of course there will be cheating, divine interferences... It allows me to run a very wide range of scenarios, from a zombie apocalypse, to creating new religions and making them fight, to... I dunno, a lot of stuff.<br /> <br /> For God : War of the Pantheons. i don't want to run the Titanomachy, the Titans are hostile antagonists, but certainly not the big bad. One of the big head of a famous pantheon (probably Zeus, with maybe Odin) wants to send humanity back to its roots, by unleashing multiple cataclysms on them, then recreating new myths to revive their worship. Of course, one faction will rebel against this, many gods will have an agenda, and a third small faction will even want to get the hell outta here and create a whole new planet with a lot of Avatars forms so they could start fresh without the killing. Basically, a big mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So! I now need inspirations for the Hero city. I need characters, NPCs. I'm not asking for whole character sheets, but mainly ideas.<br /> For now, here are some of my ideas:<br /> -One of the local frats is led by an Aesir Scion who gave blood to his brothers, and together they fight crime! ... Except that they're not great at it.<br /> -The best pub in town owes its reputation to its satyr barman. However, you really shouldn't go there if you're single and alone...<br /> -The head of the campus? Chiron's little brother, annoyed to be stuck in this boring city.<br /> -The national park nearby is led by a Scion of a hunting Deity (probably Artemis), a ranger who has taken measures to litteraly fight against poachers and polluters. With his powers, he has established himself as some sort of Lord of The Wilds, leading his team with an iron fist but how long before he takes his mission too far?<br /> -There is an underground fighting ring in the city, ran by a Valkyrie. Of course, the deaths are real.<br /> <br /> Well, here's what I have for now. It's still in its early stages, but I would like some advices or suggestions. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T17:01:02-08:00","id":787036,"title":"","content":"Hmm...how about this:<br /> <br /> The proprietresses of the town (occult) bookstore, a trio of sisters, are secretly worshipers of Hecate and/or possible mouths of Fate itself. Scions who buy from their &quot;special stock&quot; can get hints of prophecy free with their purchase that tend to be <b>very</b> relevant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T17:35:23-08:00","id":787054,"title":"","content":"As somebody who's watched (almost) every episode of Buffy growing up, the idea of a Sunnydale Hero setting is both hilarious and appealing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L8uH26GlWeo\" data-code=\"L8uH26GlWeo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/L8uH26GlWeo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, since it won't leave me alone, I have this nagging feeling like one of the NPC's should be some kind of master thief with the Trickster nature. He doesn't just steal priceless jewels and art, he leaves behind evidence that mocks and humiliates his victims just for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T00:38:30-08:00","id":787198,"title":"","content":"You could go one more step with the Buffy imitation, instead of having the city be some kind of testing ground for heroes it is located on a Hell Mouth, a gateway to the Titan realms that is currently sealed. Its presence makes fate behave in strange ways, attracts titan spawn who seek to open the gate that Ragnarok and the invasion of Earth may began, which also draws undue attention from the gods who leave several of their own spawn in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T04:38:58-08:00","id":792094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/786803-ideas-for-building-a-campaign-setting?p=787198#post787198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could go one more step with the Buffy imitation, instead of having the city be some kind of testing ground for heroes it is located on a Hell Mouth, a gateway to the Titan realms that is currently sealed. Its presence makes fate behave in strange ways, attracts titan spawn who seek to open the gate that Ragnarok and the invasion of Earth may began, which also draws undue attention from the gods who leave several of their own spawn in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about making that a bit of both - it serves as testing ground <b>because</b> it is located over a gateway to the Underworld, that can then serve as passage to the Overworld, possibly also connecting with some strange Terra Incognita or realm of unknown origin like the Demigod's portrayal of the Minotaur's Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> PS: What if the Minotaur killed by Theseus wasn't the true demigod-monster child of Pasiphae, but just one of its spawn with the many mortal youths offered to him before Theseus ended this tribute - like the ones that appear in Demigod's intro - and the &quot;original minotaur&quot; and actual demigod-monster imprisoned in the &quot;Gateway's doorstep&quot;, out of the Labyrinth, but still out of the world, for millenia? Could make for an interesting Master-style Big Bad, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}